{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31894930",
      "title": "Reacting To Incoming Notifications",
      "lectureOrder": 250,
      "videoOrder": 241,
      "sourceHash": "220337a071cd7a2cd18560ce1b3d6cab9260a5ac7cbc80fa3fe92d06f9d9b104",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 2.903,
          "en": "At the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.903,
          "end": 6.88,
          "en": "we can schedule notifications and we can then see them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.88,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "We can see them on our devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 13.16,
          "en": "But if we tap on them, nothing happens at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.16,
          "end": 15.94,
          "en": "If we interact with such a notification,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.94,
          "end": 20.6,
          "en": "we go to the app, yes, but besides that, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.6,
          "end": 22.54,
          "en": "Sometimes this is all you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.54,
          "end": 24.68,
          "en": "Sometimes the only thing that is required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.68,
          "end": 29.26,
          "en": "is that the app is opened up when a notification is tapped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.26,
          "end": 31.29,
          "en": "But sometimes, you wanna do more than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.29,
          "end": 33.58,
          "en": "Sometimes you wanna execute some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.58,
          "end": 36.56,
          "en": "in your application when a notification was tapped,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.56,
          "end": 38.68,
          "en": "or maybe when it was received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.68,
          "end": 40.763,
          "en": "No matter if it was tapped or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.042,
          "end": 45.543,
          "en": "And that's all the possible with expo notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.293,
          "end": 49.29,
          "en": "With that import, which we already have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.29,
          "end": 51.72,
          "en": "we can add some event listeners",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 54.69,
          "en": "where we listen to incoming notifications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.69,
          "end": 58.623,
          "en": "or to the user tapping on incoming notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.47,
          "end": 63.81,
          "en": "And we can register such event handlers with use effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.81,
          "end": 67.11,
          "en": "For example, use effect is a good way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.11,
          "end": 69.78999999999999,
          "en": "of adding event listeners that should be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.78999999999999,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "when this component is rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "and that maybe should be removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 76.51,
          "en": "when this component is removed from the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.51,
          "end": 77.8,
          "en": "Even though the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.8,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "will of course never be removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 82.72,
          "en": "but you could set up event listeners in any component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.72,
          "end": 85.23,
          "en": "So it is a good practice to also handle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.23,
          "end": 88.753,
          "en": "event handler removal to avoid memory leaks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.07,
          "end": 91.97,
          "en": "So here I'm calling use effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.97,
          "end": 95.07,
          "en": "Then of course use effect has to be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.07,
          "end": 97.273,
          "en": "from react though like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.12,
          "end": 101.92,
          "en": "And with it imported, we can add our effect function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.92,
          "end": 105.49000000000001,
          "en": "and our effect dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.49000000000001,
          "end": 107.69,
          "en": "Now at the moment, I have no dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.69,
          "end": 110.19,
          "en": "But here in the use effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.19,
          "end": 115.19,
          "en": "I will call notifications at notification received listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.74000000000001,
          "end": 120.44,
          "en": "So no matter whether a user tapped on a notification or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.44,
          "end": 124.49,
          "en": "this method allows us to register an event handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.49,
          "end": 127.54,
          "en": "that will be executed whenever a new notification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.54,
          "end": 129.363,
          "en": "is received by the device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.55,
          "end": 132.98,
          "en": "So here we pass a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.98,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "to add notification received listener,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 138.5,
          "en": "and here I'll just pass an anonymous arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.5,
          "end": 141.41,
          "en": "Of course you could also point at some other function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.41,
          "end": 142.993,
          "en": "that's defined somewhere else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.27,
          "end": 148.13,
          "en": "and this function will receive a notification object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.13,
          "end": 149.69,
          "en": "that contains some information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.69,
          "end": 151.77,
          "en": "about the received notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.77,
          "end": 153.59199999999998,
          "en": "And for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.59199999999998,
          "end": 157.067,
          "en": "I will just console log notification received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.99,
          "end": 164.48,
          "en": "And then below that I will console log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.48,
          "end": 166.32,
          "en": "this notification object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.32,
          "end": 169.07999999999998,
          "en": "that we're getting here automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.07999999999998,
          "end": 171.12,
          "en": "So this will be passed in automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.12,
          "end": 175.063,
          "en": "because expo will in the end call this function for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.063,
          "end": 177.756,
          "en": "You could say this function will be called for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.756,
          "end": 180.44,
          "en": "whenever a new notification is received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.44,
          "end": 183.26,
          "en": "Now, ad notification received listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.26,
          "end": 186.28,
          "en": "returns a subscription object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.28,
          "end": 188.53,
          "en": "which we can then also use for cleaning up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.53,
          "end": 191.89,
          "en": "that subscription to this event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.89,
          "end": 194.9,
          "en": "So to clean up and remove this event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.9,
          "end": 196.963,
          "en": "whenever we don't need it anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.88,
          "end": 201.09,
          "en": "We can do this by calling subscription remove,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.09,
          "end": 203.86,
          "en": "and we should call this whenever this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.86,
          "end": 208.4,
          "en": "is removed from the screen, when it's not active anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.4,
          "end": 209.65,
          "en": "Now as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.65,
          "end": 211.98,
          "en": "the app component will always be active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.98,
          "end": 214.32,
          "en": "Still, it's a good practice to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.32,
          "end": 217.24,
          "en": "that this method is called when the app is removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.24,
          "end": 218.53,
          "en": "or when the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.53,
          "end": 221.62,
          "en": "in which use effect is triggered is removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.62,
          "end": 226,
          "en": "And you can do this by returning a function from use effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226,
          "end": 229.1,
          "en": "which will be executed automatically by react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 229.1,
          "end": 233.69,
          "en": "whenever this effect is run again or cleaned up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.69,
          "end": 237.59,
          "en": "because the component in which it was placed is removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.59,
          "end": 240.42,
          "en": "and the therefore it's inside of this cleanup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.42,
          "end": 243.91,
          "en": "where we wanna call subscription remove.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.91,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "And this is just standard react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 250.083,
          "en": "It has nothing to do with react native or notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 251.52,
          "end": 255.3,
          "en": "So now with that done, with that listener added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.3,
          "end": 259.27,
          "en": "if we now trigger this notification again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.27,
          "end": 261.26,
          "en": "and it does not matter whether we do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 261.26,
          "end": 265.49,
          "en": "on Android or on iOS, once we got the notification,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.49,
          "end": 267.23,
          "en": "we can see in our terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 268.1,
          "end": 271.53,
          "en": "that we see this notification received output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.53,
          "end": 274.9,
          "en": "and then we get this notification object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.9,
          "end": 278.36,
          "en": "And as you see, it's a quite complex object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.36,
          "end": 280.24,
          "en": "with lots of data in it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 280.24,
          "end": 284.04,
          "en": "And we, for example, get the date in milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.04,
          "end": 287.05,
          "en": "We also see the request object in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.05,
          "end": 289.993,
          "en": "which contains the content of the notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.327,
          "end": 293.52,
          "en": "And there we find things like the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 295.49,
          "en": "but of course also the title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 295.49,
          "end": 298.64,
          "en": "and a couple of other fields that could have been set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 298.64,
          "end": 302.69,
          "en": "when we called scheduled notification async.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.69,
          "end": 305.61,
          "en": "You might recall that we had more properties here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 305.61,
          "end": 308.67,
          "en": "Some of these properties can now be found here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 308.67,
          "end": 311.43,
          "en": "in this received notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 311.43,
          "end": 312.82,
          "en": "We also get an identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 312.82,
          "end": 316.33,
          "en": "which is a unique ID for that notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 316.33,
          "end": 318.62,
          "en": "And with that, we can of course then also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 318.62,
          "end": 321.81,
          "en": "get any data out of this notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 321.81,
          "end": 323.64,
          "en": "And one of the most important fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 323.64,
          "end": 327.78,
          "en": "related to getting data out of the incoming notification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 327.78,
          "end": 332.78,
          "en": "is this data node which we have here in this request object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 333.33,
          "end": 335.963,
          "en": "and then in the nested content object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 337.29,
          "end": 340.72,
          "en": "This data object, this nested data object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 340.72,
          "end": 344.373,
          "en": "contains some data that's added by default by expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 345.657,
          "end": 348.87,
          "en": "We can ignore this, but we also see this data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.87,
          "end": 353.34000000000003,
          "en": "the username, and that is the data I set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.34000000000003,
          "end": 356.54,
          "en": "when I scheduled the notification before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 356.54,
          "end": 360.11,
          "en": "So this is this invisible data so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 360.11,
          "end": 364.31,
          "en": "which is carried along with the notification,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 364.31,
          "end": 366.8,
          "en": "which is not visible when the notification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 366.8,
          "end": 368.5,
          "en": "opens up on the device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 368.5,
          "end": 371.81,
          "en": "So this is not directly visible to the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 371.81,
          "end": 373.21,
          "en": "but of course it is data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 373.21,
          "end": 376.05,
          "en": "which we could now extract and use in our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 376.05,
          "end": 378.263,
          "en": "whenever a notification is received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 379.98,
          "end": 382.15,
          "en": "We could dive into this notification object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 382.15,
          "end": 385.53,
          "en": "into the request and the content object there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 389.13,
          "en": "and then into the data object to extract username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 389.13,
          "end": 390.54,
          "en": "this username field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 390.54,
          "end": 392.55,
          "en": "And we would get this username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 392.55,
          "end": 395.94,
          "en": "and we could, of course, then also console log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 395.94,
          "end": 398.13,
          "en": "this username here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 398.13,
          "end": 401.58299999999997,
          "en": "We can console log this here and extract it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 403.07,
          "end": 406.12,
          "en": "So if we do this and maybe reload everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 406.12,
          "end": 408.89,
          "en": "if I now schedule this notification again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 408.89,
          "end": 411.76,
          "en": "and we wait for it to arrive here on iOS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 411.76,
          "end": 414.28,
          "en": "the same would be true for Android though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 414.28,
          "end": 416.59000000000003,
